course: dictionary
lesson: 8077
title: Religious and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word. Its clues can help you work out what an unknown word means. «In Bradford, Tariq's dad is strict and religious and warm underneath.» Strict tells you he has firm rules, and religious describes a person who believes in a religion and follows its rules.
explain: Words ending in -ly can change meaning. «He brushes his teeth religiously» does not mean the teeth are religious. Brushing every day shows that religiously means very carefully and regularly.
explain: Other words near religious show its topic. «A hospital chaplain is a religious leader who visits patients and families.» Hospital, patients and leader all point to religion, so religious leader means someone who leads a religion.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put connected with religion in place of religious: «Tariq's dad is strict and connected with religion» still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Religious means connected with religion, the belief in a god or gods and the ways people worship.
fact: A religious person believes in a religion and follows its rules.
fact: Religiously can mean very carefully and regularly, as in «He brushes his teeth religiously».
fact: Religious phrases include religious festival, religious education (RE), religious leader and religious beliefs.
fact: In RE, pupils learn about religions such as Christianity, Islam, Judaism, Hinduism, Sikhism and Buddhism, and learn to respect people's beliefs, including people who are not religious.
exercise: In «Tariq's dad is strict and religious», what does religious describe? | Lost in the city | *Believing in a religion and following its rules | Funny and loud | Very fast
exercise: «He brushes his teeth religiously.» What does religiously mean here? | *Very carefully and regularly | Quietly, in a whisper | Very carelessly and rarely | Angrily
exercise: Which phrase names a lesson where pupils learn about many religions? | Sports day | Maths homework | *Religious education (RE) | Art club
test: «A hospital chaplain is a religious leader who visits patients and families.» What is a religious leader? | A teacher who tests spelling | A doctor who cures patients | *Someone who leads a religion and visits people in hospital | A nurse who serves dinners
test: In «Quakers worship mostly in silence», what does worship mean? | Run races in the park | *Honour a god or gods in the ways a religion does | Shout songs loudly | Eat dinner together
exam: In «"Called home" means died; it is used in American religious talk», what does the word religious tell you? | It is a rude word | It is a phrase about a sport | *The phrase comes from religious talk, so it may mean called home to God | It is a phrase about the weather
